  "section_notes": "S1 is weakened: only serious incidents (fire, thermal runaway, medical injury) are reportable, with a 72-hour regulator deadline and 5-day customer notice, excluding minor overheating/smoke. S2 is weakened: it keeps the 55 °C test but sets an 8% interim failure cap with a two-year review, above the 5% safe limit, though exact per-model results go to customers and regulators without public disclosure. S3 and S4 are acceptable (6-year retrofit, 36-month suppression), while S5 is weakened because the 8/100k threshold only triggers regulator review and possible corrective action, not mandatory recall."
